# Review routing for this repository.
#
# A pattern here REQUESTS a review; it does not require one. Branch protection decides that
# separately, and `require_code_owner_reviews` is off on `main`, so nothing in this file can make a
# merge harder. What it changes is that a pull request arrives with a reviewer already assigned
# instead of waiting to be noticed.
#
# GitHub never requests a review from the pull request's own author, so a request opened by the
# automation account routes here while one opened by the maintainer routes to nobody. That is the same
# reason the translation drains are opened by the bot: an author cannot approve their own pull
# request, so a self-authored one can only be merged by overriding branch protection — and an override
# that happens on every merge stops meaning anything.
#
# The catch-all is deliberate while there is one reviewer. Narrowing it by path would only create gaps
# that route nowhere, which is worse than routing everything to the same person. Add specific paths
# above it when there is a second reviewer to route to.
